cff-version: 1.2.0
title: Claims Layer
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-20
authors:
  - family-names: Lee
    given-names: Mun Seok
license: AGPL-3.0-only
repository-code: https://github.com/sparkainlp-x
abstract: >-
  Machine-checkable evidence passports for public claims. Each claim
  carries its kind (announcement, model, measurement, hypothesis,
  inference), an evidence tag (synthetic, reported, target, unrun),
  and machine-runnable checks (file digests, run-record values,
  textual citations). Statuses (verified, supported, unverified,
  refuted) are assigned by the checks, never by the author; a
  passport seals only when nothing is refuted and every measurement
  is verified. Combines patterns from quantum-claims-passport,
  evidence-passport, sparkholo-coherence-agent, spark-iis-api, and
  measurement-trail. A seal proves consistency and provenance, not
  ground truth.
keywords:
  - claims-verification
  - evidence-passport
  - provenance
  - misinformation
  - reproducibility
  - fail-closed
